{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Performance","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"role":"article","title":"Performance"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The binary-size budget, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle guarantee, and the re-render characteristics of the default placeholders — what’s measured, what’s guaranteed, and why."}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"],"title":"Related Documentation"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/performance"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"ScreenStates’ pitch is “small, dependency-free, drop into any screen.” This article covers the three ways that’s kept measurable rather than just assumed: a CI-enforced size budget, an audited concurrency guarantee, and a documented rendering characteristic.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"The-binary-size-budget","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The binary-size budget"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"CI builds ","type":"text"},{"code":"swift build -c release","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on every push and sums the resulting ","type":"text"},{"code":".o","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sizes for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenStates","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" target, failing the build if that total exceeds the budget committed in ","type":"text"},{"code":".github\/binary-size-budget.json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". There’s no single linked artifact to measure instead — the library product is “automatic,” and nothing in the package’s own build graph links it standalone — so the ","type":"text"},{"code":".o","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" total is the closest deterministic proxy available.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A legitimate feature addition that grows this total past the budget isn’t blocked forever: bump ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxBytes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in that file as part of the same PR, the same way a dependency lockfile gets updated alongside the change that needed it. The job never bumps it on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"The-Task-lifecycle-guarantee","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Task lifecycle guarantee"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"load","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"loadCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"loadWithRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" each store their running ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a private ","type":"text"},{"code":"currentTask","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property, read by ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Every one of those ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s captures ","type":"text"},{"code":"self","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"code":"[weak self]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not strongly — audited specifically to rule out a ","type":"text"},{"code":"self -> currentTask -> closure -> self","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" retain cycle keeping a store alive after its last external reference is dropped.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In practice, a completed ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" releases its closure’s captures on return regardless of capture style, so this mostly matters for a still-","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"running","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" operation: without ","type":"text"},{"code":"[weak self]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a store couldn’t become eligible for deallocation until that operation finished, even once every other reference to it was already gone. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the rest of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lifecycle — cancellation, overlapping calls, and the automatic cancel-on-","type":"text"},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" safety net this guarantee supports.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Re-render-characteristics-of-the-default-placeholders","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Re-render characteristics of the default placeholders"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" only ever go active once ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.